{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-quantum-ideal-gas-law","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:quantum-ideal-gas-law","kind":"proposition","title":"Quantum ideal gas law","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-pressure","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-volume","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-noether-theorem-callout"],"tags":["ideal-gas","statistical-mechanics","equation-of-state","q-anomaly","noether","hydrogen"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas","text":"quantum-ideal-gas-law.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:quantum-ideal-gas-law\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe containing <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N</code> non-interacting particle knots in a region <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U \\subset M</code>. The equation of state is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  P_q \\, V_q = N \\, T_q \\left( 1 + \\frac{\\hbar_q^2}{[2]_q} \\,\\langle \\mathfrak{S}_q \\rangle \\right).</code></pre>\n<p>Here <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\langle \\mathfrak{S}_q \\rangle</code> represents the thermal expectation of the categorical action, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[2]_q = q + q^{-1}</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"21.9.8"}
